{"id":"e11t2","name":"Payment Method Mix per Merchant","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["payments_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A payment service provider wants a wide report with one row per merchant and one amount column per payment method, to feed a dashboard.</p>\n<h3>Input</h3>\n<p><code>payments_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>payment_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>merchant_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>method</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>free text, e.g. <code>\"card\"</code>, <code>\" Card \"</code>, <code>\"WALLET\"</code>, <code>\"bank_transfer\"</code>, <code>\"crypto\"</code>; may be null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td>strictly positive, never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>status</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td><code>succeeded</code>, <code>failed</code> or <code>refunded</code> (always lowercase)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows that share a <code>payment_id</code> are exact duplicates.</p>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Only <code>succeeded</code> payments count. Each <code>payment_id</code> counts once.</li>\n<li>The method is trimmed and lowercased. <code>card</code>, <code>wallet</code> and <code>bank_transfer</code> are kept as they are; any other value, including null, becomes <code>other</code>.</li>\n<li>One output row per merchant with at least one counted payment. A merchant without any counted payment does not appear.</li>\n<li>The four amount columns always exist, even if no payment in the input uses that method; a method that a merchant did not use has an amount of <code>0.0</code>, not null.</li>\n<li>All amounts are rounded to 2 decimals. <code>card_share_pct</code> is <code>100 * card amount / total amount</code>, rounded to 1 decimal.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>Exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>merchant_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>n_payments</td>\n<td>long</td>\n<td>number of counted payments</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>card_amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>wallet_amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>bank_transfer_amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>other_amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>total_amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td>sum of the four amounts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>card_share_pct</td>\n<td>double</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>total_amount</code> descending, then <code>merchant_id</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>payments_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>payment_id</th>\n<th>merchant_id</th>\n<th>method</th>\n<th>amount</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>P1</td>\n<td>M1</td>\n<td>\"card\"</td>\n<td>100.0</td>\n<td>succeeded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P2</td>\n<td>M1</td>\n<td>\" Card \"</td>\n<td>50.0</td>\n<td>succeeded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P3</td>\n<td>M1</td>\n<td>\"wallet\"</td>\n<td>25.5</td>\n<td>succeeded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P4</td>\n<td>M1</td>\n<td>\"card\"</td>\n<td>70.0</td>\n<td>failed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P5</td>\n<td>M2</td>\n<td>\"bank_transfer\"</td>\n<td>300.0</td>\n<td>succeeded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P6</td>\n<td>M2</td>\n<td>\"crypto\"</td>\n<td>20.0</td>\n<td>succeeded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P7</td>\n<td>M2</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>10.0</td>\n<td>succeeded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P8</td>\n<td>M3</td>\n<td>\"card\"</td>\n<td>40.0</td>\n<td>refunded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P2</td>\n<td>M1</td>\n<td>\" Card \"</td>\n<td>50.0</td>\n<td>succeeded</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>merchant_id</th>\n<th>n_payments</th>\n<th>card_amount</th>\n<th>wallet_amount</th>\n<th>bank_transfer_amount</th>\n<th>other_amount</th>\n<th>total_amount</th>\n<th>card_share_pct</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>M2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>0.0</td>\n<td>0.0</td>\n<td>300.0</td>\n<td>30.0</td>\n<td>330.0</td>\n<td>0.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>M1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>150.0</td>\n<td>25.5</td>\n<td>0.0</td>\n<td>0.0</td>\n<td>175.5</td>\n<td>85.5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Function signature</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">from pyspark.sql import DataFrame\n\ndef solve(payments_df: DataFrame) -&gt; DataFrame:\n    ...\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the PySpark DataFrame API. No pandas, no <code>collect()</code>, no Python UDFs.</li>\n<li><code>payments_df</code> has up to 10^7 rows.</li>\n<li>The returned DataFrame may be empty; its 8 columns and their types must still match the specification.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import DataFrame, Window\nfrom pyspark.sql import functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(payments_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return payments_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":[],"minutes":22,"source":"Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°3, question 2","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"payments_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"payment_id string, merchant_id string, method string, amount double, status string","rows":[["P1","M1","card",100.0,"succeeded"],["P2","M1"," Card ",50.0,"succeeded"],["P3","M1","wallet",25.5,"succeeded"],["P4","M1","card",70.0,"failed"],["P5","M2","bank_transfer",300.0,"succeeded"],["P6","M2","crypto",20.0,"succeeded"],["P7","M2",null,10.0,"succeeded"],["P8","M3","card",40.0,"refunded"],["P2","M1"," Card ",50.0,"succeeded"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["merchant_id","n_payments","card_amount","wallet_amount","bank_transfer_amount","other_amount","total_amount","card_share_pct"],"rows":[["M2",3,0.0,0.